# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (Google BFF) and the /me account endpoints.
# WHEN:  At the start of every manual test session that needs a logged-in
#        user; /me endpoints whenever account behavior changes.
# WHY:   The API uses HttpOnly session cookies (BFF pattern) - Rider stores
#        the cookie from a login response automatically and sends it on all
#        following requests against the same host.
# WHERE: All environments use the Google browser flow. For authenticated
#        exploratory work, use Swagger in that same browser session.
# AUTH:  Google creates the session; the remaining requests require its cookie.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Google login start (open this URL in a browser, not Rider)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/google/start?returnUrl={{site}}/konto

### Login-failed landing (what the callback redirects to on OAuth errors)
# EXPECT: 403 ProblemDetails.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login-failed

### Refresh the session (rotates the hashed refresh token server-side)
# WHY: verify rotation + reuse detection; run twice in a row - the second
# call must still succeed because Rider stores the rotated cookie.
# NOTE: body-less writes with a session need the X-CSRF header (BFF CSRF check).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
X-CSRF: 1

### Logout (revokes the refresh-token family and clears cookies)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/logout
X-CSRF: 1

### Who am I (requires session cookie; 401 after logout)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/me

### Update my display name (validation: bounded length, not empty)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Neuer Anzeigename"
}

### Update profile - validation error variant
# EXPECT: 400 ProblemDetails with German message (empty display name).
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": ""
}

### My personal data export (GDPR Art. 20) - JSON download
GET {{host}}/api/v1/me/export

### My own reviews (all statuses, including soft-deleted)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/me/reviews

### Delete my account (GDPR) - anonymizes profile, soft-deletes reviews
# CAREFUL: irreversible for the test user; retention/legal holds still apply.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/me
X-CSRF: 1

### /me without a session - unauthorized variant
# EXPECT: 401. Run after "Logout" above.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/me
